# Markdown Formatting

- Markdown only — never raw HTML
- One `#` (H1) per file, matching the chapter/pattern title
- Proper heading hierarchy: `##` for major sections, `###` for sub-points —
  never skip a level (e.g. `#` straight to `###`)
- Wrap prose near ~100 characters per line where practical (soft wrap is fine,
  don't hard-break mid-sentence in a way that breaks rendering)
- Use tables for comparisons (complexity, pattern cheat sheets), bullet lists
  for enumerations, numbered lists only for sequential steps
- Use `---` horizontal rules between major sections within a file
- Use fenced code blocks with a language tag for pseudocode (` ```text ` or
  ` ```pseudo `), never unlabeled blocks
- Callout boxes are Markdown blockquotes with an emoji prefix (see
  `HANDBOOK_STYLE_GUIDE.md` for the fixed set: 💡 ⚠️ 🚀 🏗️ 🧠)
- No trailing whitespace, no more than one blank line in a row
- No placeholder text ("TODO", "Lorem ipsum", "...") in finished chapters —
  draft-in-progress files instead carry a single `> Status: not yet written`
  line right under the title
